b.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/deployments","created_at":"2015-04-13T18:04:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T14:39:15Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-29T14:43:56Z","git_url":"git://github.com/apache/airflow.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:apache/airflow.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow","homepage":"https://airflow.apache.org/","size":790917,"stargazers_count":47308,"watchers_count":47308,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":18214,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1927,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["airflow","apache","apache-airflow","automation","dag","data-engineering","data-integration","data-orchestrator","data-pipelines","data-science","elt","etl","machine-learning","mlops","orchestration","python","scheduler","workflow","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration"],"visibility":"public","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/73015","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73015","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73015.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73015.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n     https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0 -->\n\ncloses: #73010\n\n`S3DagBundle` stages the bundle by downloading the prefix one object at a time (`S3Hook.sync_to_local_dir`), so a bundle of N small files costs ~N GET (+N HEAD) sequential requests on every component that stages it. Under KubernetesExecutor every task instance is a fresh pod with an empty bundle directory, which puts the full staging cost on the critical path of every task start, and even a steady-state \"nothing changed\" refresh still pays a full per-object walk.\n\nThis PR adds an opt-in `archive_key` argument to `S3DagBundle`. When it is set, the bundle is staged from a single `.tar.gz` object: one `HEAD`, one `GET` with `If-Match` on that ETag, a safe unpack (`tarfile` `filter=\"data\"`), and a swap into place. Between the two renames the bundle directory is briefly absent. A failed second rename puts the previous tree back. An unchanged ETag skips the download. The ETag marker is stored beside the bundle directory (`.{name}/etag`), and leftover staging directories are removed from that same directory. Archive mode requires Python 3.11.4 or later. Constructing the bundle on an older interpreter raises `RuntimeError`.\n\n`archive_key` and `prefix` are mutually exclusive. Passing both raises at construction. When `archive_key` is set the archive is the only source of the Dags: there is no second copy to keep in sync and no fallback to a per-object sync. A missing archive fails on the refresh `HEAD` with the client's 404. A failed stage leaves the previously staged bundle in place. Publishing the archive is the deployer's job (documented: `tar -C ./dags -czf dags.tar.gz .` and `aws s3 cp`).\n\nLocal reproduction: https://github.com/aoelvp94/airflow-s3-dag-bundle-staging-demo (Airflow 3 + MinIO, 400 files / ~3 MiB). For that file set the stock path is 400 GET + 400 HEAD plus listings. This revision's cold archive path is one `head_object` and one `If-Match` GET, plus the bucket check.\n\nDesign notes:\n\n* **One class, opt-in.** No `archive_key` means nothing changes for existing users.\n* **No second copy to keep in sync.** An earlier revision fell back to the per-object sync of `prefix` when the archive failed. That needs two copies kept consistent by hand, and a transient failure on one GET turns into a full prefix walk from every component staging at that moment. Dropping the fallback also removed the prefix `LIST` probe that existed only to make the fallback safe.\n* **Deletions need no reconciliation.** The unpacked tree replaces the previous one. The previous tree stays in the staging directory until the swap succeeds, and that directory is removed afterwards.\n* **The per-object path is a separate change.** Using `get_object` instead of `download_file` would drop the per-object `HEAD`, and concurrency would cut wall-clock, but neither takes the request count below ~N. That also changes behavior for every existing `S3DagBundle` user, so it is not in this PR. The same archive shape is in review for GCS (#75566) and Azure Blob (#75657).\n\nUnit tests cover archive staging, the ETag skip, re-staging when the ETag changes, `If-Match` using the HEAD ETag, a mismatched ETag leaving the previous tree, mutual exclusion, a missing archive returning the client's 404, a corrupt archive leaving the tree, a failed swap restoring the tree, stale staging directories removed only for this bundle, a member that escapes the bundle being rejected, and `archive_key` requiring `tarfile.data_filter`. Docs are updated in `providers/amazon/docs/bundles/index.rst`.\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes (please specify the tool below)\n\nGenerated-by: Claude Code following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n\nGenerated-by: Grok in Cursor following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n\n---\n\n* Read the **[Pull Request Guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#pull-request-guidelines)** for more information. Note: commit author/co-author name and email in commits become permanently public when merged.\n* For fundamental code changes, an Airflow Improvement Proposal ([AIP](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/AIRFLOW/Airflow+Improvement+Proposals)) is needed.\n* When adding dependency, check compliance with the [ASF 3rd Party License Policy](https://www.apache.org/legal/resolved.html#category-x).\n* For significant user-facing changes create newsfragment: `{pr_number}.significant.rst`, in [airflow-core/newsfragments](https://github.com/apache/airflow/tree/main/airflow-core/newsfragments). You can add this file in a follow-up commit after the PR is created so you know the PR number.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73015/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73015/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":31053287730,"node_id":"LE_lADOAgUK288AAAABQ5YxPs8AAAAHOuuRMg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/events/31053287730","actor":{"login":"shahar1","id":60007259,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDA3MjU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60007259?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shahar1","html_url":"https://github.com/shahar1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shahar1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shahar1/following{/other_user}",